      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Um, well, I guess it's actually been a thing since I was pretty young. I hope it's okay to bring up stuff from that far back? \n\nEven in elementary school, my teachers would write little notes on my report cards. They were always really nice about it, but they'd mention that I tended to rush through my worksheets a bit, or that I'd sort of lose track of the directions they had just given us. And... I feel a little bad admitting this, because I really didn't mean to be rude, but they also said I would sometimes talk over my classmates during group work. I just got so eager to share, I think. \n\nAnd at home, my parents actually used to sit right beside me while I did my homework. If they didn't, I would just kind of wander off or start doing something else before I finished. They were really supportive about it, though! I just... I guess I've always been a little scattered like that. Is that the kind of background information you need?",
